| `dependency_audit.max_shown_chars` | integer | `500` | a whole number, 1 or more | `scripts/audit_dependencies.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `dependency_audit.max_shown_chars` row | Sets the most characters of npm's diagnostic an exit 11 line of `make fe-audit` shows. A longer diagnostic is cut before it is redacted, the word the cut lands in is dropped, and the line ends `<cut to N characters>`; the next step is still chosen from the whole diagnostic. Another value is refused with exit 14. Absent, the audit writes `[using default] dependency_audit.max_shown_chars = 500` to stderr. | which spans are hidden: the redaction rules in `docs/guides/deterministic-checks.md` section 16 | always |
